{"input":"Executable task contract:\nJSON scalar values in this task are null, boolean, integer (excluding boolean), or string. No floating point or coercion is used. Scalar equality is type-sensitive. Malformed tasks are outside the valid-task domain.\nInput: `worlds` lists `{world_id:string,facts:{fact_name:JSON_scalar}}` with distinct IDs and identical fact-key sets in every world. `observations` is an ordered list of `{fact:existing_fact_name,equals:JSON_scalar}`. `queries` is an ordered list of `{query_id:string,fact:existing_fact_name}` with distinct IDs. Start with all worlds. Each observation retains exactly currently possible worlds whose named fact equals equals with type-sensitive equality (true differs from integer 1). Record the remaining-world count after each observation. Empty beliefs remain empty, including after inconsistent observations. For each query, count the named fact's values over final surviving worlds, keeping boolean/integer/string/null values distinct. Output counts as `{value,count}` entries sorted lexicographically by each value's canonical JSON scalar encoding (ensure_ascii=false, no extra whitespace); count only values that occur. distinct_values is the number of count entries. entailed is true exactly when belief is nonempty and all surviving worlds have the same value. guaranteed is that value if entailed, otherwise null. can_reduce_uncertainty is true exactly when distinct_values>1; this reports a possible distinguishing query, not entropy. Return exactly `{surviving_worlds:[world_ids_sorted_lexicographically],belief_sizes:[integers],queries:[{query_id,counts:[{value,count}],distinct_values:integer,entailed:boolean,guaranteed:JSON_scalar,can_reduce_uncertainty:boolean}]}`. Query rows follow input order. This task uses explicit finite possible worlds, including empty beliefs.\nTask JSON:\n{\"kind\":\"belief\",\"worlds\":[{\"world_id\":\"scenario0\",\"facts\":{\"hue\":1,\"portal\":\"closed\",\"sigil\":\"unknown\"}},{\"world_id\":\"scenario1\",\"facts\":{\"hue\":true,\"portal\":\"open\",\"sigil\":\"known\"}},{\"world_id\":\"scenario2\",\"facts\":{\"hue\":\"blue\",\"portal\":\"closed\",\"sigil\":\"unknown\"}},{\"world_id\":\"scenario3\",\"facts\":{\"hue\":null,\"portal\":\"open\",\"sigil\":\"unknown\"}},{\"world_id\":\"scenario4\",\"facts\":{\"hue\":1,\"portal\":\"closed\",\"sigil\":\"known\"}},{\"world_id\":\"scenario5\",\"facts\":{\"hue\":true,\"portal\":\"open\",\"sigil\":\"unknown\"}}],\"observations\":[{\"fact\":\"hue\",\"equals\":1},{\"fact\":\"hue\",\"equals\":true}],\"queries\":[{\"query_id\":\"q0\",\"fact\":\"hue\"},{\"query_id\":\"q1\",\"fact\":\"portal\"},{\"query_id\":\"q2\",\"fact\":\"sigil\"}]}","target":{"belief_sizes":[2,0],"queries":[{"can_reduce_uncertainty":false,"counts":[],"distinct_values":0,"entailed":false,"guaranteed":null,"query_id":"q0"},{"can_reduce_uncertainty":false,"counts":[],"distinct_values":0,"entailed":false,"guaranteed":null,"query_id":"q1"},{"can_reduce_uncertainty":false,"counts":[],"distinct_values":0,"entailed":false,"guaranteed":null,"query_id":"q2"}],"surviving_worlds":[]}}
